<!-- CONVERTED — VISUALLY VERIFIED --><chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xml:id="ch16-power-series-taylor-polynomials-and-taylor-series">
  <title>Power Series, Taylor Polynomials, and Taylor Series</title>
  <shorttitle>Power Series and Taylor Series</shorttitle>

  <introduction><p>A power series is a series whose terms are powers of the input multiplied by fixed coefficients. We will determine where it converges and justify operations on it inside that interval. Taylor polynomials match derivatives at a chosen point; remainder estimates determine whether they approximate the function and whether its Taylor series represents it.</p></introduction>

